      "Build one TemporalClockSelection from the finite_hyper_clause source and span with ClockConfiguration::EventPosition { sequence_authority: test-hyper-events }.",
      "Link the graph with CheckedPackage::link, call emit_checked_with_temporal_selections, and take raw_wire(&emission) from fsl-package/src/emit/tests.rs as the complete base checked-package JSON value; raw_wire reads emission.package.bytes() without resolving operand slots. Preserve every generated node, reference, occurrence, lock member, sidecar, and source-map row.",
      "Select the unique semantic_graph node with node_tag claim and semantic_form hyperproperty; the current emitter base has its body aggregate without temporal_profile, and the mutation protocol adds the typed DefinitionRef. The base lock includes D and temporal_bindings has one row for each trace a and b."
    ],
    "mutation_protocol": "For each case, clone the entire generated raw_wire value and apply exactly the case's mutations in the order listed, then nothing else; keep every other package member and every untouched row unchanged. Operations: `set-body-temporal-profile` sets body.temporal_profile of the node selected by `where` (`unique-claim-hyperproperty-node`: the unique node with node_tag claim and semantic_form hyperproperty) to `value`, a key of profile_definitions whose `definition` object is used, or to `literal`, a JSON value written verbatim; `remove-body-temporal-profile` deletes body.temporal_profile from that node and is a no-op when it is absent, so TCB-17 stays a missing-member case whether or not the emitter writes the member; `set-body-member` sets the named body member of the node selected by `where` (`unique-temporal-clause-node`: the unique node with node_tag temporal and semantic_form temporal_clause) to `value`/`literal` as above; `set-lock-profile-selections` replaces the whole lock.profile_selections array by the listed Selection objects (T and D resolved from profile_definitions, any other entry named by its keyword kept as in the base); `set-temporal-binding-clock` matches declaration to the node's node_id, occurrence 0 and the trace. Placeholders `{hyperproperty-index}` and `{temporal-clause-index}` in a locus are the graph index of the selected node.",
    "profile_definitions": {
      "T": {"role": "temporal_profile", "definition": {"authority": "agent-ix", "identity": "filament.temporal.infinite-trace/v1"}},
      "D": {"role": "temporal_profile", "definition": {"authority": "agent-ix", "identity": "filament.temporal.event-position.false-extension/v1"}}
    }
